  "verification_notes": [
    "The fresh isolated checkout/profile run resumed after an old weather fixture was corrected: actors now stand inside the same foreground furniture span, so the test measures nearby fog perception rather than blocked sight across its edge. Physical cover behavior was unchanged.",
    "A final emergency wait guard prevents repeated sleep/cancel attempts when provisions are missing. Its 87-case suite, campaign/expansion, four-day journey, actual UI and three new persistence processes were repeated after the fix; the final exported bytes were tested separately.",
    "The campaign guide wording and font were updated before graphical regression; source, verification copy and export have the same final runtime hashes.",
    "Graphical screenshots declare altered need values and one meal as display fixtures. The separate new-start four-day journey grants no resources and issues no manual eat, drink or sleep commands.",
    "The desktop acceptance uses the real load_game API to verify restored saves remain paused; raw apply_state intentionally restores the stored pause state.",
    "All failed legacy long-run assertions are retained above; no claim that every registered check or long-term balance is green."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Windows executables are officially exported; Windows hardware and audible sound remain unverified.",
    "Exported Linux desktop continuity ran two minutes, not the default thirty-minute Windows acceptance duration.",
    "The new default-autonomy journey covers four daytime periods and three night settlements, not a full campaign or multiple long-term strategies.",
    "The old core-scene long-run policy has known failures. The additional endurance assertion collection was not certified after a harness timeout; broader long-term balance remains unfinished.",
    "Basic autonomy applies to idle residents during playable daytime. Night duty uses the existing explicit assignment and settlement system; no new real-time companion simulation is claimed.",
    "The simple model style and existing two-floor maps remain; room/door stealth and live base defense remain future work."
  ]
